# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendored native source (N-2). Byte-for-byte upstream, and git must not touch it.
#
# `* text=auto eol=lf` above normalises line endings on checkin, which is right for this
# repository's own sources and WRONG for a vendored tree: 188 files in pjproject and
# libvpx ship with CRLF, and normalising them means the committed bytes are not upstream's
# bytes. Two things then break at once — architecture rule 12's tree hash differs between
# the machine that vendored and a fresh checkout, and `the vendored tree equals
# upstream-plus-patches` (N-7) stops being true in a way no diff shows.
#
# `-text` disables all line-ending conversion. `-diff` keeps `git log -p` on a 141 MB
# import readable; the trees are reviewed as an import and as patches, never as a diff.
third_party/** -text
third_party/** linguist-vendored

# The one thing that must still be examinable, because it is what a licence review reads.
third_party/*/COPYING   -text linguist-vendored
third_party/*/LICENSE   -text linguist-vendored
third_party/*/LICENSE.* -text linguist-vendored

